rong> 1 updates, 26 insights</span>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <main class=\"container\">\n        <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n            <!-- New Products Section -->\n            <section class=\"new-products\" id=\"new-products\">\n                <div class=\"section-header\">\n                    New Products\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"empty-state\">\n                    <div class=\"empty-state-icon\">📦</div>\n                    <p>No new products found in this research cycle.</p>\n                    <p style=\"font-size: 10px; margin-top: 5px;\">Check back tomorrow for new discoveries!</p>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <div class=\"section-header\">\n                    Whitelist Updates\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases/tag/v1.3.38-vscode\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Continue v1.3.38 for VSCode\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-release\">release</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Continue released version 1.3.38 for VSCode extension featuring config.yaml improvements, session history filtering by workspace directory, and .continue/configs support. Includes dependency updates and pre-release builds for multiple platforms including Alpine Linux, macOS ARM64, and other architectures.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>📅 2026-03-27</span>\n                        <span>by Continue</span>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"feedback\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item feedback-negative\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Users experiencing rate limit errors with Claude Sonnet (429 errors) and GPT-5 (400 errors) shortly after the release\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">GitHub Issues #12057, #12056</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item feedback-positive\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Community contributed OpenRouter provider support with dynamic model loading and fuzzy search UI improvements\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">GitHub PR #8738</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item feedback-negative\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"User reports 'extension is not indexing even after giving it specific configuration' with Ollama setup on macOS (v1.2.22)\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">GitHub Issue #12067 (2026-04-07)</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item feedback-neutral\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Request for documentation on OpenRouter app identification headers that were added in recent PRs\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">GitHub Issue #12065 (2026-04-07)</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item feedback-negative\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Bug report: JSON schema of tools not being provided, causing integration issues\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">GitHub Issue #12066 (2026-04-07)</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n                <div class=\"section-header\">\n                    Technical Insights\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/google-ai-edge-gallery/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Google AI Edge Gallery - Local Gemma 4 Models on iPhone\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google released an official app for running Gemma 4 models (E2B and E4B sizes) directly on iPhone. The app works remarkably well with the 2.54GB E2B model being both fast and useful. Features include image Q&A, audio transcription (up to 30s), and 'skills' demo showing tool calling against eight interactive widgets.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-06</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">local-llms</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">gemini</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">llm-tool-use</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">mobile-ai</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-ports/releases/tag/0.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            datasette-ports 0.2 Released\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Release of datasette-ports 0.2 - a tool to find all currently running Datasette instances and list their ports. No longer requires Datasette - running 'uvx datasette-ports' now works standalone.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-06</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">developer-tools</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">python</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/openai-alums-have-been-quietly-investing-from-a-new-potentially-100m-fund/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            OpenAI Alums Launch $100M Investment Fund\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-techmedia\">TECHMEDIA</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        OpenAI alumni have been quietly investing from a new potentially $100M fund, showing continued financial activity in the AI space from former OpenAI personnel.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-06</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">investment</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">vc</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/google-quietly-releases-an-offline-first-ai-dictation-app-on-ios/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Google Quietly Launches Offline-First AI Dictation App on iOS\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-techmedia\">TECHMEDIA</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google quietly released an AI dictation app that works offline on iOS, similar to the AI Edge Gallery app for running local models.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-06</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">google</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ios</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">offline-ai</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/syntaqlite-ai/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Eight Years of Wanting, Three Months of Building with AI\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Lalit Maganti's piece on agentic engineering: spent 8 years thinking about and 3 months building syntaqlite. Key insight: AI excels at tedious work like 400+ grammar rules. Claude Code helped build the first prototype, but they eventually threw it away - AI made them procrastinate on key design decisions because refactoring felt cheap.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/05/copilot-is-for-entertainment-purposes-only-according-to-microsofts-terms-of-service/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Copilot 'For Entertainment Purposes Only' Per Microsoft Terms\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-techmedia\">TECHMEDIA</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Microsoft's terms of service indicate Copilot is 'for entertainment purposes only', raising questions about liability and production use guarantees for AI coding assistants.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">microsoft</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">copilot</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">terms-of-service</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/4/kyle-daigle/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            GitHub Activity Surging: 275 Million Commits Per Week\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub platform activity is accelerating dramatically. There were 1 billion commits in 2025. Now it's 275 million commits per week, on pace for 14 billion this year. GitHub Actions grew from 500M minutes/week in 2023 to 2.1B minutes this week. Shows massive explosion in development activity, likely driven by AI coding tools.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-04</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">github</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">github-actions</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-activity</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/04/anthropic-says-claude-code-subscribers-will-need-to-pay-extra-for-openclaw-support/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Anthropic Says Claude Code Subscribers Need Extra Payment for OpenClaw\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-techmedia\">TECHMEDIA</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic announced that Claude Code subscribers will need to pay extra for OpenClaw usage, introducing new pricing tiers for advanced coding features.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-04</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">pricing</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/vulnerability-research/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Vulnerability Research Is Cooked - AI Agents Finding Zero Days\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Thomas Ptacek's analysis: frontier models are drastically altering vulnerability research. Within months, coding agents will handle most high-impact vulnerability research. Agents excel because LLMs encode supernatural correlation across codebases, complete library of bug classes, and pattern matching abilities. Vulnerability research is 'the perfect problem for an LLM agent'.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-03</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">llm-capabilities</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/anthropic-buys-biotech-startup-coefficient-bio-in-400m-deal-reports/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Anthropic Buys Biotech Startup Coefficient Bio in $400M Deal\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-techmedia\">TECHMEDIA</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic acquires biotech startup Coefficient Bio in a $400M deal, expanding into AI applications for biotechnology research.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-03</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">acquisition</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">biotech</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/lennys-podcast/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Highlights from Lenny's Podcast on Agentic Engineering\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-discussion\">DISCUSSION</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison was a guest on Lenny Rachitsky's podcast discussing 'An AI state of the union: We've passed the inflection point, dark factories are coming, and automation timelines'. Episode covers agentic engineering, coding agents, and the current state of AI development.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-02</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">podcast</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-llm/releases/tag/0.1a6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            datasette-llm 0.1a6 Released\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Release of datasette-llm 0.1a6, an LLM integration plugin for Datasette that other plugins can depend on. Part of Simon's ongoing work building LLM tooling.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">plugins</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Agentic-MME: What Agentic Capability Really Brings to Multimodal Intelligence?\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-paper\">PAPER</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ArXiv paper exploring what agentic capabilities truly bring to multimodal intelligence systems. Investigates the unique advantages of agentic AI architectures in handling complex multimodal tasks.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Qianshan Wei et al.</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">multimodal</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">research</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            AgentHazard: Benchmark for Evaluating Harmful Behavior in Computer-Use Agents\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-paper\">PAPER</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ArXiv paper introducing AgentHazard, a benchmark designed to evaluate harmful behaviors in computer-using AI agents. Important for AI safety research as agents gain more autonomy.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Yunhao Feng et al.</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-safety</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">benchmark</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Multi-Turn Reinforcement Learning for Tool-Calling Agents\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-paper\">PAPER</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ArXiv paper on multi-turn reinforcement learning approaches for tool-calling agents with iterative reward calibration. Addresses challenges in training agents that effectively use external tools.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Wachiravit Modecrua et al.</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">reinforcement-learning</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">tool-calling</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            FoE: Forest of Errors Makes First Solution Best in Large Reasoning Models\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-paper\">PAPER</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ArXiv paper presenting FoE (Forest of Errors), a technique to make the first solution the best in large reasoning models through error-based tree approaches.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Kehan Jiang et al.</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">reasoning</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">error-handling</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            InfoSeeker: Scalable Hierarchical Parallel Agent Framework\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-paper\">PAPER</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ArXiv paper introducing InfoSeeker, a hierarchical parallel agent framework designed for efficient web information seeking. Addresses scalability in multi-agent web research systems.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Ka Yiu Lee et al.</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">web-scraping</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">hierarchical-agents</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            Automatic Textbook Formalization\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-paper\">PAPER</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ArXiv paper on automatic formalization of textbooks, using AI to convert educational content into formal mathematical representations. Important for AI education and verification.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Fabian Gloeckle et al.</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">formalization</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">education</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">math</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n                            SCRAT: Coupled Control, Structured Memory, and Verifiable Action\n                        </a>\n                        <span class=\"source source-paper\">PAPER</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ArXiv paper presenting SCRAT (Stochastic Control with Retrieval and Auditable Trajectories), drawing insights from squirrel locomotion and scatter-hoarding for agentic AI architectures with verifiable actions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>👤 Maximiliano Armesto, Christophe Kolb</span>\n                        <span>📅 2026-04-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">control</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">memory</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <p>\n                <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">API</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n            </p>\n            <p style=\"margin-top: 10px;\">\n                Report generated by Agent Code Daily - Powered by Claude Agent SDK\n            </p>\n            <p style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 10px;\">\n                © 2026 Agent Daily. All rights reserved.\n            </p>\n        </div>\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>"
}

