>\n   259→            <section class=\"new-products\">\n   260→                <h2>🆕 New Products</h2>\n   261→                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n   262→                    No new products discovered today. Check back tomorrow for the latest agentic coding tools and platforms.\n   263→                </div>\n   264→            </section>\n   265→\n   266→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   267→                <h2>📋 Whitelist Updates</h2>\n   268→\n   269→                <div class=\"item\">\n   270→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   271→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases/tag/v1.3.38-vscode\" target=\"_blank\">Continue v1.3.38 for VSCode</a>\n   272→                    </div>\n   273→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Release</div>\n   274→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   275→                        Pre-release builds available for multiple platforms including Alpine Linux, macOS ARM64, and other architectures.\n   276→                    </div>\n   277→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   278→                        <span>📅 2026-03-27</span>\n   279→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   280→                    </div>\n   281→                    <div class=\"community-feedback negative\">\n   282→                        <div class=\"quote\">Users experiencing rate limit errors with Claude Sonnet (429 errors) and GPT-5 (400 errors)</div>\n   283→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">Source: GitHub Issues #12057, #12056</div>\n   284→                    </div>\n   285→                    <div class=\"community-feedback positive\">\n   286→                        <div class=\"quote\">Community contributed OpenRouter provider support with dynamic model loading and fuzzy search UI improvements</div>\n   287→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">Source: GitHub PR #8738</div>\n   288→                    </div>\n   289→                </div>\n   290→            </section>\n   291→\n   292→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   293→                <h2>💡 Technical Insights</h2>\n   294→\n   295→                <div class=\"item\">\n   296→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   297→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/google-ai-edge-gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Google AI Edge Gallery - Local Gemma 4 Models on iPhone</a>\n   298→                    </div>\n   299→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   300→                        Google released an official app for running Gemma 4 models directly on iPhone with image Q&A, audio transcription, and tool calling widgets.\n   301→                    </div>\n   302→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   303→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   304→                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n   305→                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n   306→                    </div>\n   307→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   308→                        <span class=\"tag\">local-llms</span>\n   309→                        <span class=\"tag\">gemini</span>\n   310→                        <span class=\"tag\">mobile-ai</span>\n   311→                    </div>\n   312→                </div>\n   313→\n   314→                <div class=\"item\">\n   315→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   316→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-ports/releases/tag/0.2\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-ports 0.2 Released</a>\n   317→                    </div>\n   318→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   319→                        Tool to find all currently running Datasette instances and list their ports. Now works standalone without Datasette.\n   320→                    </div>\n   321→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   322→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   323→                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n   324→                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n   325→                    </div>\n   326→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   327→                        <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n   328→                        <span class=\"tag\">developer-tools</span>\n   329→                        <span class=\"tag\">python</span>\n   330→                    </div>\n   331→                </div>\n   332→\n   333→                <div class=\"item\">\n   334→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   335→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/openai-alums-have-been-quietly-investing-from-a-new-potentially-100m-fund/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Alums Launch $100M Investment Fund</a>\n   336→                    </div>\n   337→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   338→                        OpenAI alumni have been quietly investing from a new potentially $100M fund, showing continued financial activity in the AI space.\n   339→                    </div>\n   340→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   341→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   342→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   343→                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n   344→                    </div>\n   345→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   346→                        <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n   347→                        <span class=\"tag\">investment</span>\n   348→                        <span class=\"tag\">vc</span>\n   349→                    </div>\n   350→                </div>\n   351→\n   352→                <div class=\"item\">\n   353→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   354→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/google-quietly-releases-an-offline-first-ai-dictation-app-on-ios/\" target=\"_blank\">Google Quietly Launches Offline-First AI Dictation App on iOS</a>\n   355→                    </div>\n   356→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   357→                        Google quietly released an AI dictation app that works offline on iOS, similar to the AI Edge Gallery app for running local models.\n   358→                    </div>\n   359→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   360→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   361→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   362→                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n   363→                    </div>\n   364→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   365→                        <span class=\"tag\">google</span>\n   366→                        <span class=\"tag\">ios</span>\n   367→                        <span class=\"tag\">offline-ai</span>\n   368→                    </div>\n   369→                </div>\n   370→\n   371→                <div class=\"item\">\n   372→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   373→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/iran-threatens-stargate-ai-data-centers/\" target=\"_blank\">Iran Threatens 'Stargate' AI Data Centers</a>\n   374→                    </div>\n   375→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   376→                        Geopolitical tensions involving AI infrastructure as Iran threatens 'Stargate' AI data centers, highlighting strategic importance of AI facilities.\n   377→                    </div>\n   378→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   379→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   380→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   381→                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n   382→                    </div>\n   383→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   384→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-infrastructure</span>\n   385→                        <span class=\"tag\">geopolitics</span>\n   386→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                </div>\n   389→\n   390→                <div class=\"item\">\n   391→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   392→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/syntaqlite-ai/\" target=\"_blank\">Eight Years of Wanting, Three Months of Building with AI</a>\n   393→                    </div>\n   394→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   395→                        AI excels at tedious work but can lead to deferred architectural decisions. Key lesson: AI is great for low-level details but can make you procrastinate on key design decisions.\n   396→                    </div>\n   397→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   398→                        <span>Simon Willison (citing Lalit Maganti)</span>\n   399→                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n   400→                        <span>📅 Apr 5</span>\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   403→                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   404→                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n   405→                        <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   406→                    </div>\n   407→                </div>\n   408→\n   409→                <div class=\"item\">\n   410→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   411→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/05/japan-is-proving-experimental-physical-ai-is-ready-for-the-real-world/\" target=\"_blank\">Japan Proving Experimental Physical AI Ready for Real World</a>\n   412→                    </div>\n   413→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   414→                        In Japan, robots aren't coming for jobs - they're filling jobs nobody wants. Shows practical deployment of physical AI in real-world scenarios.\n   415→                    </div>\n   416→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   417→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   418→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   419→                        <span>📅 Apr 5</span>\n   420→                    </div>\n   421→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   422→                        <span class=\"tag\">physical-ai</span>\n   423→                        <span class=\"tag\">robotics</span>\n   424→                        <span class=\"tag\">japan</span>\n   425→                    </div>\n   426→                </div>\n   427→\n   428→                <div class=\"item\">\n   429→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   430→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/05/copilot-is-for-entertainment-purposes-only-according-to-microsofts-terms-of-service/\" target=\"_blank\">Copilot 'For Entertainment Purposes Only' Per Microsoft Terms</a>\n   431→                    </div>\n   432→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   433→                        Microsoft's terms of service indicate Copilot is 'for entertainment purposes only', raising questions about liability and production use guarantees for AI coding assistants.\n   434→                    </div>\n   435→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   436→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   437→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   438→                        <span>📅 Apr 5</span>\n   439→                    </div>\n   440→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   441→                        <span class=\"tag\">microsoft</span>\n   442→                        <span class=\"tag\">copilot</span>\n   443→                        <span class=\"tag\">liability</span>\n   444→                    </div>\n   445→                </div>\n   446→\n   447→                <div class=\"item\">\n   448→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   449→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/4/kyle-daigle/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Activity Surging: 275 Million Commits Per Week</a>\n   450→                    </div>\n   451→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   452→                        GitHub platform activity is accelerating dramatically. On pace for 14 billion commits this year if growth remains linear. Massive explosion in development activity, likely driven by AI coding tools.\n   453→                    </div>\n   454→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   455→                        <span>Simon Willison (citing Kyle Daigle)</span>\n   456→                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n   457→                        <span>📅 Apr 4</span>\n   458→                    </div>\n   459→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   460→                        <span class=\"tag\">github</span>\n   461→                        <span class=\"tag\">github-actions</span>\n   462→                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-activity</span>\n   463→                    </div>\n   464→                </div>\n   465→\n   466→                <div class=\"item\">\n   467→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   468→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/04/anthropic-says-claude-code-subscribers-will-need-to-pay-extra-for-openclaw-support/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Says Claude Code Subscribers Need Extra Payment for OpenClaw</a>\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   471→                        Anthropic announced that Claude Code subscribers will need to pay extra for OpenClaw usage, introducing new pricing tiers for advanced coding features.\n   472→                    </div>\n   473→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   474→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   475→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   476→                        <span>📅 Apr 4</span>\n   477→                    </div>\n   478→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   479→                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n   480→                        <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   481→                        <span class=\"tag\">pricing</span>\n   482→                    </div>\n   483→                </div>\n   484→\n   485→                <div class=\"item\">\n   486→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   487→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/openai-executive-shuffle-new-roles-coo-brad-lightcap-fidji-simo-kate-rouch/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Executive Shuffle: New Roles for COO Brad Lightcap</a>\n   488→                    </div>\n   489→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   490→                        OpenAI executive shuffle includes new role for COO Brad Lightcap to lead 'special projects', along with new roles for Fidji Simo and Kate Rouch.\n   491→                    </div>\n   492→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   493→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   494→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   495→                        <span>📅 Apr 3</span>\n   496→                    </div>\n   497→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   498→                        <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n   499→                        <span class=\"tag\">executives</span>\n   500→                        <span class=\"tag\">leadership</span>\n   501→                    </div>\n   502→                </div>\n   503→\n   504→                <div class=\"item\">\n   505→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   506→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/anthropic-buys-biotech-startup-coefficient-bio-in-400m-deal-reports/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Buys Biotech Startup Coefficient Bio in $400M Deal</a>\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   509→                        Anthropic acquires biotech startup Coefficient Bio in a $400M deal, expanding into AI applications for biotechnology research.\n   510→                    </div>\n   511→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   512→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   513→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   514→                        <span>📅 Apr 3</span>\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   517→                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n   518→                        <span class=\"tag\">acquisition</span>\n   519→                        <span class=\"tag\">biotech</span>\n   520→                    </div>\n   521→                </div>\n   522→\n   523→                <div class=\"item\">\n   524→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   525→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/ai-companies-are-building-huge-natural-gas-plants-to-power-data-centers-what-could-go-wrong/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Companies Building Huge Natural Gas Plants for Data Centers</a>\n   526→                    </div>\n   527→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   528→                        AI companies are constructing massive natural gas power plants to support energy-intensive data centers, raising environmental and infrastructure concerns.\n   529→                    </div>\n   530→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   531→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   532→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   533→                        <span>📅 Apr 3</span>\n   534→                    </div>\n   535→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   536→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-infrastructure</span>\n   537→                        <span class=\"tag\">energy</span>\n   538→                        <span class=\"tag\">environment</span>\n   539→                    </div>\n   540→                </div>\n   541→\n   542→                <div class=\"item\">\n   543→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   544→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/vulnerability-research/\" target=\"_blank\">Vulnerability Research Is Cooked - AI Agents Finding Zero Days</a>\n   545→                    </div>\n   546→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   547→                        Within months, coding agents will handle most high-impact vulnerability research. LLMs excel at this: supernatural correlation across codebases, complete library of bug classes, pattern matching, and endless search without boredom.\n   548→                    </div>\n   549→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   550→                        <span>Simon Willison (citing Thomas Ptacek)</span>\n   551→                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n   552→                        <span>📅 Apr 3</span>\n   553→                    </div>\n   554→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   555→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n   556→                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   557→                        <span class=\"tag\">llm-capabilities</span>\n   558→                    </div>\n   559→                </div>\n   560→\n   561→                <div class=\"item\">\n   562→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   563→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/anthropic-ramps-up-its-political-activities-with-a-new-pac/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Ramps Up Political Activities with New PAC</a>\n   564→                    </div>\n   565→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   566→                        Anthropic is increasing its political engagement by forming a new Political Action Committee, joining other AI companies in political lobbying efforts.\n   567→                    </div>\n   568→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   569→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   570→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   571→                        <span>📅 Apr 3</span>\n   572→                    </div>\n   573→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   574→                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n   575→                        <span class=\"tag\">politics</span>\n   576→                        <span class=\"tag\">lobbying</span>\n   577→                    </div>\n   578→                </div>\n   579→\n   580→                <div class=\"item\">\n   581→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   582→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/02/openai-acquires-tbpn-the-buzzy-founder-led-business-talk-show/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Acquires TBPN Business Talk Show</a>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   585→                        OpenAI acquires TBPN, the buzzy founder-led business talk show, showing expansion into media content.\n   586→                    </div>\n   587→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   588→                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n   589→                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n   590→                        <span>📅 Apr 2</span>\n   591→                    </div>\n   592→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   593→                        <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n   594→                        <span class=\"tag\">acquisition</span>\n   595→                        <span class=\"tag\">media</span>\n   596→                    </div>\n   597→                </div>\n   598→\n   599→                <div class=\"item\">\n   600→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   601→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/lennys-podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlights from Lenny's Podcast on Agentic Engineering</a>\n   602→                    </div>\n   603→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   604→                        Simon Willison was a guest on Lenny Rachitsky's podcast discussing 'An AI state of the union: We've passed the inflection point, dark factories are coming, and automation timelines'.\n   605→                    </div>\n   606→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   607→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   608→                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n   609→                        <span>📅 Apr 2</span>\n   610→                    </div>\n   611→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   612→                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n   613→                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   614→                        <span class=\"tag\">podcast</span>\n   615→                    </div>\n   616→                </div>\n   617→\n   618→                <div class=\"item\">\n   619→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   620→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-llm/releases/tag/0.1a6\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-llm 0.1a6 Released</a>\n   621→                    </div>\n   622→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   623→                        Release of datasette-llm 0.1a6, an LLM integration plugin for Datasette that other plugins can depend on.\n   624→                    </div>\n   625→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   626→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   627→                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n   628→                        <span>📅 Apr 1</span>\n   629→                    </div>\n   630→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   631→                        <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n   632→                        <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n   633→                        <span class=\"tag\">plugins</span>\n   634→                    </div>\n   635→                </div>\n   636→\n   637→                <div class=\"item\">\n   638→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   639→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\">Agentic-MME: What Agentic Capability Really Brings to Multimodal Intelligence?</a>\n   640→                    </div>\n   641→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   642→                        ArXiv paper exploring what agentic capabilities truly bring to multimodal intelligence systems.\n   643→                    </div>\n   644→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   645→                        <span>Qianshan Wei et al.</span>\n   646→                        <span class=\"source paper\">Paper</span>\n   647→                        <span>📅 Apr 1</span>\n   648→                    </div>\n   649→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   650→                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-ai</span>\n   651→                        <span class=\"tag\">multimodal</span>\n   652→                        <span class=\"tag\">research</span>\n   653→                    </div>\n   654→                </div>\n   655→\n   656→                <div class=\"item\">\n   657→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   658→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\">AgentHazard: Benchmark for Evaluating Harmful Behavior in Computer-Use Agents</a>\n   659→                    </div>\n   660→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   661→                        ArXiv paper introducing AgentHazard, a benchmark designed to evaluate harmful behaviors in computer-using AI agents.\n   662→                    </div>\n   663→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   664→                        <span>Yunhao Feng et al.</span>\n   665→                        <span class=\"source paper\">Paper</span>\n   666→                        <span>📅 Apr 1</span>\n   667→                    </div>\n   668→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   669→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-safety</span>\n   670→                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n   671→                        <span class=\"tag\">benchmark</span>\n   672→                    </div>\n   673→                </div>\n   674→\n   675→                <div class=\"item\">\n   676→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   677→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\">Multi-Turn Reinforcement Learning for Tool-Calling Agents</a>\n   678→                    </div>\n   679→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   680→                        ArXiv paper on multi-turn reinforcement learning approaches for tool-calling agents with iterative reward calibration.\n   681→                    </div>\n   682→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   683→                        <span>Wachiravit Modecrua et al.</span>\n   684→                        <span class=\"source paper\">Paper</span>\n   685→                        <span>📅 Apr 1</span>\n   686→                    </div>\n   687→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   688→                        <span class=\"tag\">reinforcement-learning</span>\n   689→                        <span class=\"tag\">tool-calling</span>\n   690→                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n   691→                    </div>\n   692→                </div>\n   693→\n   694→                <div class=\"item\">\n   695→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   696→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\">FoE: Forest of Errors Makes First Solution Best in Large Reasoning Models</a>\n   697→                    </div>\n   698→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   699→                        ArXiv paper presenting FoE (Forest of Errors), a technique to make the first solution the best in large reasoning models through error-based tree approaches.\n   700→                    </div>\n   701→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   702→                        <span>Kehan Jiang et al.</span>\n   703→                        <span class=\"source paper\">Paper</span>\n   704→                        <span>📅 Apr 1</span>\n   705→                    </div>\n   706→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   707→                        <span class=\"tag\">reasoning</span>\n   708→                        <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n   709→                        <span class=\"tag\">error-handling</span>\n   710→                    </div>\n   711→                </div>\n   712→\n   713→                <div class=\"item\">\n   714→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   715→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\">InfoSeeker: Scalable Hierarchical Parallel Agent Framework for Web Information Seeking</a>\n   716→                    </div>\n   717→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   718→                        ArXiv paper introducing InfoSeeker, a hierarchical parallel agent framework designed for efficient web information seeking.\n   719→                    </div>\n   720→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   721→                        <span>Ka Yiu Lee et al.</span>\n   722→                        <span class=\"source paper\">Paper</span>\n   723→                        <span>📅 Apr 1</span>\n   724→                    </div>\n   725→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   726→                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n   727→                        <span class=\"tag\">web-scraping</span>\n   728→                        <span class=\"tag\">scalability</span>\n   729→                    </div>\n   730→                </div>\n   731→\n   732→                <div class=\"item\">\n   733→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   734→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\">Automatic Textbook Formalization</a>\n   735→                    </div>\n   736→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   737→                        ArXiv paper on automatic formalization of textbooks, using AI to convert educational content into formal mathematical representations.\n   738→                    </div>\n   739→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   740→                        <span>Fabian Gloeckle et al.</span>\n   741→                        <span class=\"source paper\">Paper</span>\n   742→                        <span>📅 Apr 1</span>\n   743→                    </div>\n   744→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   745→                        <span class=\"tag\">formalization</span>\n   746→                        <span class=\"tag\">education</span>\n   747→                        <span class=\"tag\">math</span>\n   748→                    </div>\n   749→                </div>\n   750→\n   751→                <div class=\"item\">\n   752→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   753→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\" target=\"_blank\">SCRAT: Coupled Control, Structured Memory, and Verifiable Action in Agentic AI</a>\n   754→                    </div>\n   755→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   756→                        ArXiv paper presenting SCRAT (Stochastic Control with Retrieval and Auditable Trajectories), drawing insights from squirrel locomotion and scatter-hoarding for agentic AI architectures.\n   757→                    </div>\n   758→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   759→                        <span>Maximiliano Armesto, Christophe Kolb</span>\n   760→                        <span class=\"source paper\">Paper</span>\n   761→                        <span>📅 Apr 1</span>\n   762→                    </div>\n   763→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   764→                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-ai</span>\n   765→                        <span class=\"tag\">control</span>\n   766→                        <span class=\"tag\">bio-inspired</span>\n   767→                    </div>\n   768→                </div>\n   769→            </section>\n   770→        </main>\n   771→\n   772→        <footer>\n   773→            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n   774→            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   775→            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a>\n   776→            <a href=\"#\">GitHub</a>\n   777→            <span>•</span>\n   778→            <span>Generated automatically from research data</span>\n   779→        </footer>\n   780→    </div>\n   781→</body>\n   782→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
